WF-45 — Rebook Handler

## Summary

- Purpose: Handles a REBOOK request. A state guard at the head prevents an invalid status regression: only users in a rebook-eligible state are moved back to `payment_pending`; users mid-flow (payment_submitted / consultation_active) get an explanatory message and NO state change.
- Inputs:
  - `phoneNumber` — E.164 string, required. Routes all lookups + sends.
  - `userId` — integer, optional (passed by some callers; not consumed — the inline SELECT is keyed on phoneNumber).
- Outputs: For a rebook-eligible user — status set back to `payment_pending` + a WhatsApp interactive payment prompt. For payment_submitted / consultation_active — an explanatory message, no UPDATE. For pre-form/no-record — a "let's get you set up" + Flow CTA, no UPDATE (defensive-only — see note).
- State Transitions: rebook-eligible (payment_pending / consultation_closed / opted_out-re-entry / unknown) → payment_pending. Other states: none.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp).
- Called by: WF-20 (REBOOK keyword — existing users), WF-43 (btn_rebook + rebook_intent). *(WF-44 no longer calls WF-45 — it became a pure recorder per safety-net decision #11.)*
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-45 (TD-BMX-01, safety-net §REBOOK-by-stage):**
  - ADDED a state-classifier guard before any UPDATE — branch by computed state (see Step 3). The prior WF-45 always UPDATEd to payment_pending regardless of current state.
  - Design rule preserved: does NOT call WF-52; reuses the existing consult Slack channel (`slack_channel_id` stays on the row).
- **Notes:**
  - **Pre-form/no-record branch is defensive-only (dead in practice):** BMX-06 preempts pre-form/new REBOOK upstream (WF-23/WF-21 literal-keyword steps), and WF-20 only runs for existing users — so no live path reaches WF-45 without a `users` row. The branch self-heals if one ever does. 3 live branches remain (payment_submitted, consultation_active, happy-path) + 1 defensive.
  - **Copy is subject to user review at build** (verify verbatim).

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-20 or WF-43 with `phoneNumber`.
Step 2: SELECT id, name, phone_number, status FROM chinmay_astro.users WHERE phone_number = phoneNumber LIMIT 1.
Step 3: Branch on the user's current state:
  - No row found (pre-form / no record) → go to Step 4 (defensive — let's get you set up).
  - status == 'payment_submitted' → go to Step 5 (under review, wait).
  - status == 'consultation_active' → go to Step 6 (active consult — ask to close first).
  - else (payment_pending / consultation_closed / opted_out-re-entry / unknown) → go to Step 7 (happy-path rebook).
Step 4: Send a "let's get you set up" message + the WhatsApp Flow form CTA via WF-50. No UPDATE. End.
  - Copy (LOCKED 2026-05-30, user-approved): body.text = "Welcome! 🙏 To book a consultation with Dr. Chinmay Mujumdar, please share your birth details using the form below to get started." + WhatsApp Flow form CTA (header "Birth Details Form", flowId 2260297164474475, CTA "Fill Details", policy URL chinmaymujumdar.com/privacy-policy) — same Flow params as WF-21/WF-23.
Step 5: Send the under-review clarifier via WF-50. No UPDATE. End.
  - Copy (LOCKED 2026-05-30, user-approved): "Your payment is still being reviewed — please wait for confirmation before booking again. We'll be in touch shortly. 🙏"
Step 6: Send the active-consultation clarifier via WF-50. No UPDATE. End.
  - Copy (LOCKED 2026-05-30, user-approved): "You're currently in an active consultation. Please complete it first — Dr. Chinmay will close it once you're done, and you can rebook after that. 🙏"
Step 7: UPDATE chinmay_astro.users SET status = 'payment_pending', stage = NULL, updated_at = NOW() WHERE phone_number = phoneNumber. Then build the interactive payment prompt:
  - body.text = "Welcome back, {user.name}! 🙏\n\nYour birth details are already on file, so we can get started right away.\n\n*Payment Information:*\nAmount: ₹500\n\nPlease send ₹500 via GPay / PhonePe / any UPI app to: +91-9653240263 (Chinmay Mujumdar). Once done, tap the button below:"
  - buttons: [ { id: "payment_completed", title: "Payment Completed" } ]
  Call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'interactive', interactivePayload: <payload> }`. End.
